8. OpenShift Editions
Red Hat provides different editions of OpenShift for different needs.
They differ based on:
•	management
•	features
•	infrastructure
________________________________________
9. Development / Learning Editions
1 OpenShift Local
Runs OpenShift on a local machine.
Used for:
•	learning
•	testing
•	development
Not used in production.
________________________________________
2 Developer Sandbox
Free 30-day OpenShift access on Red Hat cloud.
Used for:
•	practice
•	development
•	testing applications
________________________________________
10. Production OpenShift Editions
These are used in real production environments.
________________________________________
Managed OpenShift
Managed means:
•	cloud provider + Red Hat manage cluster
Examples:
•	AWS OpenShift
•	Azure OpenShift
•	Google Cloud OpenShift
•	IBM Cloud OpenShift
Benefits:
•	easy setup
•	automatic updates
•	infrastructure managed by provider
Less control but less maintenance.
________________________________________
Self-Managed OpenShift
Company installs OpenShift themselves.
Can run on:
•	on-premise servers
•	private cloud
•	public cloud VMs
Benefits:
•	full control
•	customization
But requires more management effort.
________________________________________
11. OpenShift Product Editions
There are four major OpenShift product tiers.
________________________________________
1 OpenShift Virtualization Engine
Used mainly for virtual machines.
Features:
•	deploy virtual machines
•	manage VMs
•	scaling VMs
•	virtualization console
Useful when companies migrate VM workloads to OpenShift.
________________________________________
2 OpenShift Kubernetes Engine
Basic OpenShift platform.
Includes:
•	Kubernetes
•	security hardening
•	enterprise stability
•	RHEL CoreOS
Used for container orchestration only.
________________________________________
3 OpenShift Container Platform
Most commonly used enterprise edition.
Includes everything from Kubernetes Engine plus:
•	developer console
•	CI/CD pipelines
•	monitoring
•	logging
•	cost management
•	metering
Also includes additional tools:
Feature	Technology
Serverless	Knative
Service Mesh	Istio
Pipelines	Tekton
GitOps	Argo CD
This is the standard OpenShift enterprise platform.
________________________________________
4 OpenShift Platform Plus
Most advanced edition.
Includes everything from Container Platform plus:
•	Advanced Cluster Management
•	Advanced Cluster Security
•	Quay Container Registry
Used for large enterprise multi-cluster environments.
________________________________________
12. Red Hat Insights Advisor
Insights is a cluster analysis tool.
It helps administrators:
•	detect cluster issues
•	recommend fixes
•	improve performance
•	maintain security
________________________________________
How it works
1 Cluster sends data using Insights Operator
2 Data uploaded to:
Red Hat Hybrid Cloud Console
3 System analyzes cluster health.
4 Provides recommendations.
